msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2387
msgid "{ref}`llvm.stackrestore.p5 <int_stackrestore>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2389
msgid "{ref}`llvm.get.fpmode.i32 <int_get_fpmode>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2390
msgid ""
"The natural floating-point mode type is i32. This is implemented by "
"extracting relevant bits out of the MODE register with s_getreg_b32. The "
"first 10 bits are the core floating-point mode. Bits 12:18 are the exception "
"mask. On gfx9+, bit 23 is FP16_OVFL. Bitfields not relevant to floating-"
"point instructions are 0s."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2396
msgid "{ref}`llvm.get.rounding<int_get_rounding>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2397
msgid ""
"AMDGPU supports two separately controllable rounding modes depending on the "
"floating-point type. One controls float, and the other controls both double "
"and half operations. If both modes are the same, returns one of the standard "
"return values. If the modes are different, returns one of {ref}`12 extended "
"values <amdgpu-rounding-mode-enumeration-values-table>` describing the two "
"modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2402
msgid ""
"To nearest, ties away from zero is not a supported mode. The raw rounding "
"mode values in the MODE register do not exactly match the FLT_ROUNDS values, "
"so a conversion is performed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2404
msgid "{ref}`llvm.set.rounding<int_set_rounding>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2405
msgid ""
"Input value expected to be one of the valid results from "
"'`llvm.get.rounding`'. Rounding mode is undefined if not passed a valid "
"input. This should be a wave uniform value. In case of a divergent input "
"value, the first active lane's value will be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2409
msgid "{ref}`llvm.get.fpenv<int_get_fpenv>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2410
msgid ""
"Returns the current value of the AMDGPU floating point environment. This "
"stores information related to the current rounding mode, denormalization "
"mode, enabled traps, and floating point exceptions. The format is a 64-bit "
"concatenation of the MODE and TRAPSTS registers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2413
msgid "{ref}`llvm.set.fpenv<int_set_fpenv>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2414
msgid "Sets the floating point environment to the specified state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2415
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.readfirstlane"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2416
msgid ""
"Provides direct access to v_readfirstlane_b32. Returns the value in the "
"lowest active lane of the input operand. Currently implemented for i16, i32, "
"float, half, bfloat, \\<2 x i16>, \\<2 x half>, \\<2 x bfloat>, i64, double, "
"pointers, multiples of the 32-bit vectors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2419
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.readlane"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2420
msgid ""
"Provides direct access to v_readlane_b32. Returns the value in the specified "
"lane of the first input operand. The second operand specifies the lane to "
"read from. Currently implemented for i16, i32, float, half, bfloat, \\<2 x "
"i16>, \\<2 x half>, \\<2 x bfloat>, i64, double, pointers, multiples of the "
"32-bit vectors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2424
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.writelane"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2425
msgid ""
"Provides direct access to v_writelane_b32. Writes value in the first input "
"operand to the specified lane of divergent output. The second operand "
"specifies the lane to write. Currently implemented for i16, i32, float, "
"half, bfloat, \\<2 x i16>, \\<2 x half>, \\<2 x bfloat>, i64, double, "
"pointers, multiples of the 32-bit vectors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2429
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.wave.reduce.umin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2430
msgid ""
"Performs an arithmetic unsigned min reduction on the unsigned values "
"provided by each lane in the wavefront. Intrinsic takes a hint for reduction "
"strategy using second operand 0: Target default preference, 1: `Iterative "
"strategy`, and 2: `DPP`. If the target does not support the DPP operations "
"(e.g. gfx6/7), reduction will be performed using default iterative strategy. "
"Intrinsic is implemented for i32 and i64 types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2434
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.wave.reduce.min"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2435
msgid ""
"Similar to `llvm.amdgcn.wave.reduce.umin`, but performs a signed min "
"reduction on signed integers. Intrinsic is implemented for i32 and i64 types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2437
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.wave.reduce.fmin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2438
msgid ""
"Similar to `llvm.amdgcn.wave.reduce.umin`, but performs a floating point min "
"reduction on floating point values. Intrinsic is implemented for float and "
"double types. Intrinsic is modelled similar to `llvm.minnum` intrinsic. For "
"a reduction between two NAN values, a NAN is returned. For a reduction "
"between a NAN and a number, the number is returned. -0.0 \\< +0.0 is true "
"for this reduction. The ordering behaviour of SNANs is non-deterministic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2444
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.wave.reduce.umax"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2445
msgid ""
"Performs an arithmetic unsigned max reduction on the unsigned values "
"provided by each lane in the wavefront. Intrinsic takes a hint for reduction "
"strategy using second operand 0: Target default preference, 1: `Iterative "
"strategy`, and 2: `DPP`. If the target does not support the DPP operations "
"(e.g. gfx6/7), reduction will be performed using default iterative strategy. "
"Intrinsic is implemented for i32 and i64 types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2449
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.wave.reduce.max"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2450
msgid ""
"Similar to `llvm.amdgcn.wave.reduce.umax`, but performs a signed max "
"reduction on signed integers. Intrinsic is implemented for i32 and i64 types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2452
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.wave.reduce.fmax"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2453
msgid ""
"Similar to `llvm.amdgcn.wave.reduce.umax`, but performs a floating point max "
"reduction on floating point values. Intrinsic is implemented for float and "
"double types. Intrinsic is modelled similar to `llvm.maxnum` intrinsic. For "
"a reduction between two NAN values, a NAN is returned. For a reduction "
"between a NAN and a number, the number is returned. -0.0 \\< +0.0 is true "
"for this reduction. The ordering behaviour of SNANs is non-deterministic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2459
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.wave.reduce.add"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2460
msgid ""
"Performs an arithmetic add reduction on the signed/unsigned values provided "
"by each lane in the wavefront. Intrinsic takes a hint for reduction strategy "
"using second operand 0: Target default preference, 1: `Iterative strategy`, "
"and 2: `DPP`. If the target does not support the DPP operations (e.g. "
"gfx6/7), reduction will be performed using default iterative strategy. "
"Intrinsic is implemented for signed/unsigned i32 and i64 types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2464
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.wave.reduce.fadd"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2465
msgid ""
"Similar to `llvm.amdgcn.wave.reduce.add`, but performs a floating point add "
"reduction on floating point values. Intrinsic is implemented for float and "
"double types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2467
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.wave.reduce.sub"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2468
msgid ""
"Performs an arithmetic sub reduction on the signed/unsigned values provided "
"by each lane in the wavefront. Intrinsic takes a hint for reduction strategy "
"using second operand 0: Target default preference, 1: `Iterative strategy`, "
"and 2: `DPP`. If the target does not support the DPP operations (e.g. "
"gfx6/7), reduction will be performed using default iterative strategy. "
"Intrinsic is implemented for signed/unsigned i32 and i64 types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2472
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.wave.reduce.fsub"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2473
msgid ""
"Similar to `llvm.amdgcn.wave.reduce.sub`, but performs a floating point sub "
"reduction on floating point values. Intrinsic is implemented for float and "
"double types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2475
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.wave.reduce.and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2476
msgid ""
"Performs a bitwise-and reduction on the values provided by each lane in the "
"wavefront. Intrinsic takes a hint for reduction strategy using second "
"operand 0: Target default preference, 1: `Iterative strategy`, and 2: `DPP`. "
"If the target does not support the DPP operations (e.g. gfx6/7), reduction "
"will be performed using default iterative strategy. Intrinsic is implemented "
"for i32 and i64 types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2480
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.wave.reduce.or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2481
msgid ""
"Similar to `llvm.amdgcn.wave.reduce.and`, but performs a bitwise-or "
"reduction on the values provided by each wavefront. Intrinsic is implemented "
"for i32 and i64 types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2483
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.wave.reduce.xor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2484
msgid ""
"Similar to `llvm.amdgcn.wave.reduce.and`, but performs a bitwise-xor "
"reduction on the values provided by each wavefront. Intrinsic is implemented "
"for i32 and i64 types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2486
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.permlane16"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2487
msgid ""
"Provides direct access to v_permlane16_b32. Performs arbitrary gather-style "
"operation within a row (16 contiguous lanes) of the second input operand. "
"The third and fourth inputs must be scalar values. These are combined into a "
"single 64-bit value representing lane selects used to swizzle within each "
"row. Currently implemented for i16, i32, float, half, bfloat, \\<2 x i16>, "
"\\<2 x half>, \\<2 x bfloat>, i64, double, pointers, multiples of the 32-bit "
"vectors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2492
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.permlanex16"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2493
msgid ""
"Provides direct access to v_permlanex16_b32. Performs arbitrary gather-style "
"operation across two rows of the second input operand (each row is 16 "
"contiguous lanes). The third and fourth inputs must be scalar values. These "
"are combined into a single 64-bit value representing lane selects used to "
"swizzle within each row. Currently implemented for i16, i32, float, half, "
"bfloat, \\<2 x i16>, \\<2 x half>, \\<2 x bfloat>, i64, double, pointers, "
"multiples of the 32-bit vectors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2498
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.permlane64"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2499
msgid ""
"Provides direct access to v_permlane64_b32. Performs a specific permutation "
"across lanes of the input operand where the high half and low half of a "
"wave64 are swapped. Performs no operation in wave32 mode. Currently "
"implemented for i16, i32, float, half, bfloat, \\<2 x i16>, \\<2 x half>, "
"\\<2 x bfloat>, i64, double, pointers, multiples of the 32-bit vectors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2503
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.wave.match.b32"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2504
msgid ""
"Provides direct access to v_wave_match_b32. Returns a 32-bit mask whose bit "
"N is set when lane N is active and its first operand equals the current "
"lane's second operand. Passing the same value as both operands yields the "
"mask of active lanes sharing that value. In wave64 mode each 32-lane half is "
"handled independently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2508
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.exclusive.scan.\\*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2509
msgid ""
"Provides direct access to the v_exclusive_scan\\_\\* instructions. Performs "
"an exclusive prefix scan of the first input operand across a subgroup of "
"lanes, selected by the mask in the second operand. Each lane receives the "
"reduction of the earlier lanes in its subgroup, so the lowest lane gets the "
"identity value. In wave64 mode the two halves of the wave are scanned "
"independently. The operation is part of the name (sum, xor, or, and, min, "
"max). Sum takes an extra i1 clamp operand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2515
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.udot2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2516
msgid ""
"Provides direct access to v_dot2_u32_u16 across targets which support such "
"instructions. This performs an unsigned dot product with two v2i16 operands, "
"summed with the third i32 operand. The i1 fourth operand is used to clamp "
"the output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2519
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.udot4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2520
msgid ""
"Provides direct access to v_dot4_u32_u8 across targets which support such "
"instructions. This performs an unsigned dot product with two i32 operands "
"(holding a vector of 4 8bit values), summed with the third i32 operand. The "
"i1 fourth operand is used to clamp the output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2523
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.udot8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2524
msgid ""
"Provides direct access to v_dot8_u32_u4 across targets which support such "
"instructions. This performs an unsigned dot product with two i32 operands "
"(holding a vector of 8 4bit values), summed with the third i32 operand. The "
"i1 fourth operand is used to clamp the output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2527
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.sdot2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2528
msgid ""
"Provides direct access to v_dot2_i32_i16 across targets which support such "
"instructions. This performs a signed dot product with two v2i16 operands, "
"summed with the third i32 operand. The i1 fourth operand is used to clamp "
"the output. When applicable (e.g. no clamping), this is lowered into "
"v_dot2c_i32_i16 for targets which support it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2532
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.sdot4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2533
msgid ""
"Provides direct access to v_dot4_i32_i8 across targets which support such "
"instructions. This performs a signed dot product with two i32 operands "
"(holding a vector of 4 8bit values), summed with the third i32 operand. The "
"i1 fourth operand is used to clamp the output. When applicable (i.e. no "
"clamping / operand modifiers), this is lowered into v_dot4c_i32_i8 for "
"targets which support it. RDNA3 does not offer v_dot4_i32_i8, and rather "
"offers v_dot4_i32_iu8 which has operands to hold the signedness of the "
"vector operands. Thus, this intrinsic lowers to the signed version of this "
"instruction for gfx11 targets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2539
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.sdot8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2540
msgid ""
"Provides direct access to v_dot8_u32_u4 across targets which support such "
"instructions. This performs a signed dot product with two i32 operands "
"(holding a vector of 8 4bit values), summed with the third i32 operand. The "
"i1 fourth operand is used to clamp the output. When applicable (i.e. no "
"clamping / operand modifiers), this is lowered into v_dot8c_i32_i4 for "
"targets which support it. RDNA3 does not offer v_dot8_i32_i4, and rather "
"offers v_dot4_i32_iu4 which has operands to hold the signedness of the "
"vector operands. Thus, this intrinsic lowers to the signed version of this "
"instruction for gfx11 targets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2546
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.sudot4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2547
msgid ""
"Provides direct access to v_dot4_i32_iu8 on gfx11 targets. This performs dot "
"product with two i32 operands (holding a vector of 4 8bit values), summed "
"with the fifth i32 operand. The i1 sixth operand is used to clamp the "
"output. The i1s preceding the vector operands decide the signedness."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2551
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.sudot8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2552
msgid ""
"Provides direct access to v_dot8_i32_iu4 on gfx11 targets. This performs dot "
"product with two i32 operands (holding a vector of 8 4bit values), summed "
"with the fifth i32 operand. The i1 sixth operand is used to clamp the "
"output. The i1s preceding the vector operands decide the signedness."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2556
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.sched.barrier"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2557
msgid ""
"Controls the types of instructions that may be allowed to cross the "
"intrinsic during instruction scheduling. The parameter is a mask for the "
"instruction types that can cross the intrinsic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2560
msgid "0x0000: No instructions may be scheduled across sched_barrier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2561
msgid ""
"0x0001: All, non-memory, non-side-effect producing instructions may be "
"scheduled across sched_barrier, *i.e.* allow ALU instructions to pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2562
msgid "0x0002: VALU instructions may be scheduled across sched_barrier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2563
msgid "0x0004: SALU instructions may be scheduled across sched_barrier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2564
msgid "0x0008: MFMA/WMMA instructions may be scheduled across sched_barrier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2565
msgid ""
"0x0010: All VMEM instructions may be scheduled across sched_barrier. This "
"includes LDSDMA instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2567
msgid ""
"0x0020: VMEM read instructions may be scheduled across sched_barrier. This "
"does not include LDSDMA loads, even though they also read from global "
"memory; only loads targeting VGPRs are classified as VMEM read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2569
msgid ""
"0x0040: VMEM write instructions may be scheduled across sched_barrier. This "
"does not include LDSDMA stores, even though they also write to global "
"memory; only stores sourcing from VGPRs are classified as VMEM write."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2571
msgid ""
"0x0080: All DS instructions may be scheduled across sched_barrier. This "
"includes LDSDMA instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2573
msgid "0x0100: All DS read instructions may be scheduled across sched_barrier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2574
msgid ""
"0x0200: All DS write instructions may be scheduled across sched_barrier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2575
msgid ""
"0x0400: All Transcendental (e.g. V_EXP) instructions may be scheduled across "
"sched_barrier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2576
msgid "0x0800: All LDSDMA instructions may be scheduled across sched_barrier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2577
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.sched.group.barrier"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2578
msgid ""
"Creates schedule groups with specific properties to create custom scheduling "
"pipelines. The ordering between groups is enforced by the instruction "
"scheduler. The intrinsic applies to the code that precedes the intrinsic. "
"The intrinsic takes three values that control the behavior of the schedule "
"groups."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2583
msgid ""
"Mask : Classify instruction groups using the llvm.amdgcn.sched_barrier mask "
"values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2584
msgid "Size : The number of instructions that are in the group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2585
msgid "SyncID : Order is enforced between groups with matching values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2587
msgid ""
"The mask can include multiple instruction types. It is undefined behavior to "
"set values beyond the range of valid masks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2590
msgid ""
"Combining multiple sched_group_barrier intrinsics enables an ordering of "
"specific instruction types during instruction scheduling. For example, the "
"following enforces a sequence of 1 VMEM read, followed by 1 VALU "
"instruction, followed by 5 MFMA instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2593
msgid ""
"`// 1 VMEM read` `__builtin_amdgcn_sched_group_barrier(32, 1, 0)` `// 1 "
"VALU` `__builtin_amdgcn_sched_group_barrier(2, 1, 0)` `// 5 MFMA` "
"`__builtin_amdgcn_sched_group_barrier(8, 5, 0)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2599
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.iglp.opt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2600
msgid ""
"An **experimental** intrinsic for instruction group level parallelism. The "
"intrinsic implements predefined instruction scheduling orderings. The "
"intrinsic applies to the surrounding scheduling region. The intrinsic takes "
"a value that specifies the strategy. The compiler implements two strategies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2606
msgid "Interleave DS and MFMA instructions for small GEMM kernels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2607
msgid "Interleave DS and MFMA instructions for single wave small GEMM kernels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2608
msgid ""
"Interleave TRANS and MFMA instructions, as well as their VALU and DS "
"predecessors, for attention kernels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2609
msgid ""
"Interleave TRANS and MFMA instructions, with no predecessor interleaving, "
"for attention kernels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2611
msgid ""
"Only one iglp_opt intrinsic may be used in a scheduling region. The iglp_opt "
"intrinsic cannot be combined with sched_barrier or sched_group_barrier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2614
msgid "The iglp_opt strategy implementations are subject to change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2615
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.s.getpc"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2616
msgid ""
"Provides access to the s_getpc_b64 instruction, but with the return value "
"sign-extended from the width of the underlying PC hardware register even on "
"processors where the s_getpc_b64 instruction returns a zero-extended value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2617
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.implicit.buffer.ptr"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2618
msgid ""
"Returns the implicit buffer pointer. This is pointer is passed in the first "
"two user SGPRs of graphics and compute shaders for the `mesa3d` OS on "
"targets without architected flat scratch. The backend uses it to set up the "
"scratch buffer resource. It is an error to use for other ABIs, for kernels "
"and non-entry functions, and on targets with architected flat scratch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2624
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.ballot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2625
msgid ""
"Returns a bitfield(i32 or i64) containing the result of its i1 argument in "
"all active lanes, and zero in all inactive lanes. Provides a way to convert "
"i1 in LLVM IR to i32 or i64 lane mask - bitfield used by hardware to control "
"active lanes when used in EXEC register. For example, ballot(i1 true) return "
"EXEC mask."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2628
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.mfma.scale.f32.16x16x128.f8f6f4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2629
msgid ""
"Emit `v_mfma_scale_f32_16x16x128_f8f6f4` to set the scale factor. The last 4 "
"operands correspond to the scale inputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2632
msgid "2-bit byte index to use for each lane for matrix A"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2633
msgid "Matrix A scale values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2634
msgid "2-bit byte index to use for each lane for matrix B"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2635
msgid "Matrix B scale values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2636
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.mfma.scale.f32.32x32x64.f8f6f4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2637
msgid "Emit `v_mfma_scale_f32_32x32x64_f8f6f4`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2638
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.permlane16.swap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2639
msgid ""
"Provide direct access to `v_permlane16_swap_b32` instruction on supported "
"targets. Swaps the values across lanes of first 2 operands. Odd rows of the "
"first operand are swapped with even rows of the second operand (one row is "
"16 lanes). Returns a pair for the swapped registers. The first element of "
"the return corresponds to the swapped element of the first argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2644
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.permlane32.swap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2645
msgid ""
"Provide direct access to `v_permlane32_swap_b32` instruction on supported "
"targets. Swaps the values across lanes of first 2 operands. Rows 2 and 3 of "
"the first operand are swapped with rows 0 and 1 of the second operand (one "
"row is 16 lanes). Returns a pair for the swapped registers. The first "
"element of the return corresponds to the swapped element of the first "
"argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2650
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.mov.dpp"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2651
msgid ""
"The llvm.amdgcn.mov.dpp.\\`\\<type>\\` intrinsic represents the mov.dpp "
"operation in AMDGPU. This operation is being deprecated and can be replaced "
"with llvm.amdgcn.update.dpp."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2653
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.update.dpp"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2654
msgid ""
"The llvm.amdgcn.update.dpp.\\`\\<type>\\` intrinsic represents the "
"update.dpp operation in AMDGPU. It takes an old value, a source operand, a "
"DPP control operand, a row mask, a bank mask, and a bound control. Various "
"data types are supported, including, bf16, f16, f32, f64, i16, i32, i64, p0, "
"p3, p5, v2f16, v2f32, v2i16, v2i32, v2p0, v3i32, v4i32, v8f16. This "
"operation is equivalent to a sequence of v_mov_b32 operations. It is "
"preferred over llvm.amdgcn.mov.dpp.\\`\\<type>\\` for future use. "
"`llvm.amdgcn.update.dpp.<type> <old> <src> <dpp_ctrl> <row_mask> <bank_mask> "
"<bound_ctrl>` Should be equivalent to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2661
msgid "`v_mov_b32 <dest> <old>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2662
msgid "`v_mov_b32 <dest> <src> <dpp_ctrl> <row_mask> <bank_mask> <bound_ctrl>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2663
msgid "{ref}`llvm.prefetch <int_prefetch>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2664
msgid ""
"Implemented on gfx1250, ignored on earlier targets. First argument is flat, "
"global, or constant address space pointer. Any other address space is not "
"supported. On gfx125x generates flat_prefetch_b8 or global_prefetch_b8 and "
"brings data to GL2. Second argument is rw and currently ignored. Can be 0 or "
"1. Third argument is locality, 0-3. Translates to memory scope:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2673
msgid "0 - SCOPE_SYS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2674
msgid "1 - SCOPE_DEV"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2675
msgid "2 - SCOPE_SE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2676
msgid "3 - SCOPE_SE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2678
msgid ""
"Note that SCOPE_CU is not generated and not safe on an invalid address. "
"Fourth argument is cache type:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2681
msgid "0 - Instruction cache, currently ignored and no code is generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2682
msgid "1 - Data cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2684
msgid "Instruction cache prefetches are unsafe on invalid address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2685
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.s.barrier"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2686
msgid ""
"Performs a barrier *arrive* operation immediately followed by a barrier "
"*wait* operation on the *workgroup barrier* object. see {ref}`amdgpu-amdhsa-"
"execution-barriers`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2687
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.s.barrier.init"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2688
msgid ""
"Performs a barrier *init* operation on the barrier *object* determined by "
"the first operand. See {ref}`amdgpu-amdhsa-execution-barriers`. Available "
"starting GFX12.5."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2691
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.s.barrier.signal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2692
msgid ""
"Performs a barrier *arrive* operation on the barrier *object* determined by "
"the `i32` immediate argument. See {ref}`amdgpu-amdhsa-execution-barriers`. "
"Available starting GFX12."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2695
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.s.barrier.signal.var"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2696
msgid ""
"Performs a barrier *arrive* operation on the barrier *object* determined by "
"the first argument. The second argument is an `i32` immediate *expected "
"count*. The *expected count* of the barrier *object* is only set when the "
"argument is not zero, and when the barrier *object* is a *named barrier "
"object*. See {ref}`amdgpu-amdhsa-execution-barriers`. Available starting "
"GFX12."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2701
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.s.barrier.signal.isfirst"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2702
msgid ""
"Performs a barrier *arrive* operation on the barrier *object* determined by "
"the `i32` immediate argument. Returns `i1 1` if the wave is running in a "
"workgroup, and it was the first wave to *arrive* at the barrier *object*, "
"otherwise returns `i1 0`. See {ref}`amdgpu-amdhsa-execution-barriers`. "
"Available starting GFX12."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2706
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.s.barrier.wait"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2707
msgid ""
"Performs a barrier *wait* operation on the barrier *object* determined by "
"the `i16` immediate argument. If waiting on a *named barrier object*, this "
"instruction always waits on the last *named barrier object* that the thread "
"has *joined*, even if it is different from the argument. See {ref}`amdgpu-"
"amdhsa-execution-barriers`. Available starting GFX12."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2711
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.s.barrier.join"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2712
msgid ""
"Performs a barrier *join* operation on the barrier *object* determined by "
"the first operand. See {ref}`amdgpu-amdhsa-execution-barriers`. Available "
"starting GFX12.5."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2715
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.s.barrier.leave"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2716
msgid ""
"Performs a barrier *drop* operation. See {ref}`amdgpu-amdhsa-execution-"
"barriers`. Available starting GFX12.5."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2719
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.flat.load.monitor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2720
msgid ""
"Available on GFX12.5 only. Corresponds to `flat_load_monitor_b32/64/128` "
"(`.b32/64/128` suffixes) instructions. For the purposes of the memory model, "
"this is an atomic load operation in the generic (flat) address space."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2724 ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2734
msgid "This intrinsic has 3 operands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2726
msgid "Flat pointer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2727 ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2737
msgid ""
"{ref}`Load Atomic Ordering<amdgpu-intrinsics-c-abi-atomic-memory-ordering-"
"operand>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2728 ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2738
msgid ""
"{ref}`Synchronization Scope<amdgpu-intrinsics-syncscope-metadata-operand>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2729
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.global.load.monitor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2730
msgid ""
"Available on GFX12.5 only. Corresponds to `global_load_monitor_b32/64/128` "
"(`.b32/64/128` suffixes) instructions. For the purposes of the memory model, "
"this is an atomic load operation in the global address space."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2736
msgid "Global pointer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2739
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.ds.atomic.barrier.arrive.rtn.b64"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2740
msgid ""
"Available starting GFX12.5. Corresponds to "
"`ds_atomic_barrier_arrive_rtn_b64`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2743
msgid ""
"For the purposes of the memory model, this is a monotonic atomic read-modify-"
"write operation in the local address space."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2745
msgid "This intrinsic has 2 operands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2747 ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2759
msgid "Local pointer to the LDS barrier data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2748
msgid ""
"Update value; the pending count of the barrier will be decremented by this "
"value (generally 1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2750
msgid ""
"Returns the LDS barrier data as it was before this operation was executed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2751
msgid "llvm.amdgcn.ds.atomic.async.barrier.arrive.b64"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2752
msgid ""
"Available starting GFX12.5. Corresponds to "
"`ds_atomic_async_barrier_arrive_b64`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2755
msgid ""
"For the purposes of the memory model, this is an asynchronous monotonic "
"atomic read-modify-write operation in the local address space."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2757
msgid "This intrinsic has 1 operand:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2763
msgid "List AMDGPU intrinsics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2768
msgid "'`llvm.amdgcn.av`' Intrinsics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2770
msgid ""
"The '`llvm.amdgcn.av`' intrinsics perform {ref}`store-available<amdgpu-store-"
"available>` and {ref}`load-visible<amdgpu-load-visible>` operations on flat "
"or global memory with *scope* supplied as a metadata argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2775
msgid ""
"The pointer argument can be a global pointer (`addrspace(1)`) or a flat "
"pointer (`addrspace(0)`). Global pointers select `global_load`/ "
"`global_store` instructions; flat pointers select `flat_load`/ `flat_store` "
"instructions. The cache policy bits are the same in both cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2800
msgid "Implementation Details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2802
msgid ""
"This section is informational and for **internal reference only**. Users "
"should not rely on the expansions described below. The only reliable user-"
"level guarantees are those provided by the {ref}`AMDGPU memory model<amdgpu-"
"memmodel>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2806
msgid ""
"The tables below show the cache policy bits for global pointer variants. "
"Flat pointer variants use the corresponding `flat_load`/`flat_store` "
"instructions with the same cache policy bits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:2810
msgid ""
"**TODO:** Currently the compiler does not support WGP mode on gfx12+. Hence, "
"`\"workgroup\"` scope currently maps to CU scope (no bits). When WGP mode is "
"enabled this should map to `scope:SCOPE_SE`."
msgstr ""

