#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3520
msgid ""
"The following ABI conventions apply to all calling conventions that are used "
"for callable functions (i.e. those that do not correspond to hardware entry "
"points):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3523
msgid ""
"On entry to a function the dependency counters (`VMcnt`, `LOADcnt` etc.) are "
"in an indeterminate state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3525
msgid ""
"On return from a function, all dependency counters must be zero except for "
"`VScnt`/`STOREcnt` or `VMcnt`/`LOADcnt` if the only outstanding operations "
"are `global_inv` or `buffer_inv`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3529
msgid ""
"For entry points, the ABI conventions are dictated by the hardware behavior "
"at wave launch and wave termination:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3532
msgid ""
"When a wave is launched the shader can assume that all dependency counters "
"are zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUUsage.md:3534
msgid ""
"The shader can leave the dependency counters in any state before terminating "
"the wave (e.g. with `s_endpgm`)."
msgstr ""

